---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Evidence" description="What the arena actually has, generated straight from the data — fighters, datasets, published predictions and boards per league.">
  <p class="eyebrow" style="margin-bottom:0.4rem">OVOS Plugin Arena · Completeness</p>
  <h1 style="font-size:clamp(1.8rem,5vw,2.6rem);margin-bottom:0.35rem">Evidence</h1>
  <p style="max-width:66ch">
    This page is generated from the same data the site publishes — no hand-typed
    numbers. It exists so an outside reviewer can check, league by league, what
    is actually in place versus what is still a gap: how many fighters are
    registered, how many datasets, how many of those datasets have <em>published</em>
    predictions on Hugging Face, and how many benchmark boards and ELO
    leaderboards exist as a result. Where a league has fighters but few or no
    published predictions, that shows up as a gap here — not a rounded-up number.
  </p>

  <div id="ev-loading" class="card" aria-live="polite">Loading evidence…</div>
  <div id="ev-empty" class="card" style="display:none">
    Try another league or language. No evidence data yet — run <code>arena.cli export-evidence</code> (wired into
    the <code>assemble.yml</code> action) to generate <code>data/evidence.json</code>.
  </div>

  <div id="ev-app" style="display:none">
    <div id="ev-totals" class="ev-totals" role="group" aria-label="Arena-wide totals"></div>

    <h2>Per league</h2>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table id="ev-table">
        <caption class="sr-only">Completeness per league: fighters, registered datasets, datasets with published predictions, benchmark boards, and ELO leaderboards.</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">League</th>
            <th scope="col">Fighters</th>
            <th scope="col">Datasets</th>
            <th scope="col">With predictions</th>
            <th scope="col">Benchmark boards</th>
            <th scope="col">ELO leaderboards</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody id="ev-tbody"></tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2>Fighter coverage, per league</h2>
    <p style="max-width:66ch">
      Dataset-level coverage above can hide fighter-level gaps: a league can have
      a published benchmark board and still have registered fighters with zero
      rows on it. This table counts, per league, how many registered fighters
      actually appear in at least one benchmark board or battles pool
      ("on boards") versus how many do not yet ("ghosts"). A ghost is a
      registered-but-not-yet-benchmarked fighter — most reflect sweeps still in
      progress, not a hidden failure. This is computed offline from the
      committed data dir only; it cannot see in-flight Hugging Face uploads.
    </p>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table id="ev-fighters-table">
        <caption class="sr-only">Fighter coverage per league: registered fighters, fighters on boards, and ghost fighters.</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">League</th>
            <th scope="col">Registered</th>
            <th scope="col">On boards</th>
            <th scope="col">Ghosts</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody id="ev-fighters-tbody"></tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2>Published predictions, per dataset</h2>
    <p style="max-width:66ch">
      Every dataset a league claims to score against, linked to its Hugging Face
      predictions repo. <span class="ev-gap-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> marks
      a dataset that is registered but has no published predictions yet — no
      benchmark board, no ELO seed for it.
    </p>
    <div id="ev-links"></div>

    <h2>Verify it yourself</h2>
    <ul role="list" class="ev-verify-list" id="ev-verify"></ul>

    <p id="ev-generated" class="ev-generated"></p>
  </div>

  <style is:global>
    .ev-totals {
      display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.9rem;
      margin: 1.5rem 0 2rem;
    }
    .ev-stat {
      flex: 1 1 160px;
      background: linear-gradient(180deg, var(--surface-2) 0%, var(--surface) 100%);
      border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius);
      padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
    }
    .ev-stat .n {
      display: block; font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 700;
      font-size: 1.9rem; color: var(--text); line-height: 1.1;
    }
    .ev-stat .l {
      display: block; margin-top: 0.3rem; font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--muted);
      text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    }
    .table-scroll { overflow-x: auto; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
    #ev-table td.num, #ev-table th.num { text-align: right; }
    #ev-table td { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
    .ev-gap { color: var(--tie); font-weight: 700; }
    .ev-gap-dot {
      display: inline-block; width: 0.55em; height: 0.55em; border-radius: 50%;
      background: var(--tie); vertical-align: middle;
    }
    .ev-league-links { margin-bottom: 1.4rem; }
    .ev-league-links h3 {
      font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 600; font-size: 1rem;
      margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
    }
    .ev-league-links ul { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
    .ev-league-links li {
      display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 0.5rem;
      padding: 0.35rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
      font-size: 0.88rem;
    }
    .ev-league-links li:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
    .ev-verify-list { padding-left: 1.2rem; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
    .ev-verify-list li { margin-bottom: 0.5rem; color: var(--muted); }
    .ev-generated { font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--muted); }
  </style>

  <script>
    const BASE = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith('/') ? import.meta.env.BASE_URL : import.meta.env.BASE_URL + '/';

    function escapeHtml(s: unknown): string {
      return String(s).replace(/[&<>"']/g, c => (
        { '&': '&amp;', '<': '&lt;', '>': '&gt;', '"': '&quot;', "'": '&#39;' } as Record<string, string>
      )[c]);
    }

    fetch(BASE + 'data/evidence.json')
      .then(r => r.ok ? r.json() : null).catch(() => null)
      .then(data => {
        document.getElementById('ev-loading')!.style.display = 'none';
        if (!data || !Array.isArray(data.leagues) || !data.leagues.length) {
          document.getElementById('ev-empty')!.style.display = 'block';
          return;
        }
        document.getElementById('ev-app')!.style.display = 'block';
        renderTotals(data);
        renderTable(data.leagues);
        renderFightersTable(data.leagues);
        renderLinks(data.leagues);
        renderVerify();
        renderGeneratedAt(data.generated_at);
      });

    function renderTotals(data: any) {
      const totals = data.totals || {};
      const fc = totals.fighter_coverage || {};
      const stats: [string, string][] = [
        [String(totals.fighters ?? '—'), 'Fighters registered'],
        [String(totals.datasets ?? '—'), 'Eval datasets registered'],
        [String(totals.spec_requirements ?? '—'), 'Spec requirements (R#)'],
        [String((data.leagues || []).length), 'Leagues'],
        [String(fc.ghosts ?? '—'), 'Ghost fighters (registered, no rows yet)'],
      ];
      const box = document.getElementById('ev-totals')!;
      box.innerHTML = stats.map(([n, l]) => `
        <div class="ev-stat"><span class="n">${escapeHtml(n)}</span><span class="l">${escapeHtml(l)}</span></div>
      `).join('');
    }

    function ghostCell(ghosts: number, registered: number): string {
      const text = String(ghosts);
      return ghosts > 0
        ? `<span class="ev-gap" title="${ghosts} of ${registered} registered fighters have no rows on any benchmark board or battles pool yet">${escapeHtml(text)}</span>`
        : escapeHtml(text);
    }

    function renderFightersTable(leagues: any[]) {
      const tbody = document.getElementById('ev-fighters-tbody')!;
      tbody.innerHTML = leagues.map(l => {
        const fc = l.fighter_coverage || {};
        return `
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">${escapeHtml(l.label || l.id)}</th>
            <td class="num">${escapeHtml(fc.registered ?? 0)}</td>
            <td class="num">${escapeHtml(fc.on_boards ?? 0)}</td>
            <td class="num">${ghostCell(fc.ghosts ?? 0, fc.registered ?? 0)}</td>
          </tr>
        `;
      }).join('');
    }

    function gapCell(have: number, total: number): string {
      const text = `${have}/${total}`;
      return have < total
        ? `<span class="ev-gap" title="${have} of ${total} datasets have published predictions">${escapeHtml(text)}</span>`
        : escapeHtml(text);
    }

    function renderTable(leagues: any[]) {
      const tbody = document.getElementById('ev-tbody')!;
      tbody.innerHTML = leagues.map(l => `
        <tr>
          <th scope="row">${escapeHtml(l.label || l.id)}</th>
          <td class="num">${escapeHtml(l.fighters)}</td>
          <td class="num">${escapeHtml(l.datasets)}</td>
          <td class="num">${gapCell(l.datasets_with_predictions, l.datasets)}</td>
          <td class="num">${escapeHtml(l.benchmark_boards)}</td>
          <td class="num">${escapeHtml(l.elo_leaderboards)}</td>
        </tr>
      `).join('');
    }

    function renderLinks(leagues: any[]) {
      const box = document.getElementById('ev-links')!;
      box.innerHTML = leagues.map(l => {
        const links = l.predictions_links || [];
        if (!links.length) {
          return `
            <div class="ev-league-links">
              <h3>${escapeHtml(l.label || l.id)}</h3>
              <p style="margin:0;font-size:0.85rem">No registered datasets with a predictions repo yet.</p>
            </div>`;
        }
        const items = links.map((link: any) => `
          <li>
            ${link.has_predictions ? '' : '<span class="ev-gap-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>'}
            <span><code>${escapeHtml(link.dataset_id)}</code></span>
            ${link.has_predictions
              ? `<a href="${escapeHtml(link.url)}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">${escapeHtml(link.predictions_hf)}</a>`
              : `<span class="ev-gap-repo">${escapeHtml(link.predictions_hf)}</span>`}
            ${link.has_predictions ? '' : '<span style="color:var(--muted);font-size:0.8rem">— registered, no predictions published</span>'}
          </li>
        `).join('');
        return `
          <div class="ev-league-links">
            <h3>${escapeHtml(l.label || l.id)}</h3>
            <ul role="list">${items}</ul>
          </div>`;
      }).join('');
    }

    function renderVerify() {
      const list = document.getElementById('ev-verify')!;
      list.innerHTML = `
        <li>Read the normative spec: <a href="https://github.com/OpenVoiceOS/ovos-plugin-arena/blob/dev/docs/SPECIFICATION.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">docs/SPECIFICATION.md</a> — every R-number counted above is defined there.</li>
        <li>Read how ratings and benchmarks are computed: <a href="${BASE}methodology/">Methodology</a>.</li>
        <li>Check that a replayed vote log never touches the network or changes with re-runs: <a href="https://github.com/OpenVoiceOS/ovos-plugin-arena/blob/dev/tests/test_tally_fraud.py" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">tests/test_tally_fraud.py</a> (offline replay-purity tests). CI-gated proof that replay reproduces the published leaderboards byte-for-field runs on every push to <code>dev</code> and daily via <a href="https://github.com/OpenVoiceOS/ovos-plugin-arena/actions/workflows/replay-proof.yml" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><img src="https://github.com/OpenVoiceOS/ovos-plugin-arena/actions/workflows/replay-proof.yml/badge.svg" alt="Replay proof status" style="vertical-align:middle;height:1em" /></a> (<a href="https://github.com/OpenVoiceOS/ovos-plugin-arena/blob/dev/.github/workflows/replay-proof.yml" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">replay-proof.yml</a>).</li>
        <li>Regenerate this page's data yourself: <code>python -m arena.cli export-evidence</code> — it reads only the registry and the committed data dir, nothing hand-typed.</li>
      `;
    }

    function renderGeneratedAt(ts: string) {
      const el = document.getElementById('ev-generated')!;
      if (!ts) { el.textContent = ''; return; }
      el.textContent = `Generated at ${ts}`;
    }
  </script>
</Base>
